WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.736
-Ninja, you are one of the most
popular streamers on the planet.

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.672
But you just made a big switch,

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.941
'cause you were over at Twitch
for a while.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.175
Now you're at Mixer.
-Yes.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.910
-Why the switch,
and do you like it?

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.478
What's happening?
-I absolutely love it, man.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:13.980
And for people that don't know,

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.615
Microsoft is a,
you know, owns Xbox,

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:18.284
one of the biggest gaming
companies in the world.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.585
-Yeah.
-They own Mixer,

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:21.587
so I've already had a lot
of incredible opportunities

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.623
switching over to Mixer,
when it comes to actually,

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.324
you know, getting early access
to video games

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.093
and being able to stream games
for other people.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.429
And it's, you know, it's really
good as an influencer.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:32.031
So, recently, "Gears of War 5"
came out.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.199
-Incredible game.
-Whoo!

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.268
-And I was able to get that game
a little early

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.002
and stream the campaign.
-You got a little, "Ooh!"

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:38.704
-"Ooh!" That's all you need
is a, "Ooh!"

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:40.272
-"Woof!" Yeah, there's a dog
in our audience, yeah.

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:42.375
-That's what it's all about.
It's all about that, "Ooh!"

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.643
-That's all you need. Yeah.
-That's all I need.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.111
-That's all you need.
-I don't need much.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.647
-Oh, what -- So you get all
the games before they come out?

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:50.116
-Not necessarily all the games.
Just a couple, and I, you know,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.218
there's a lot of other big
things that are in the works

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.320
with other, you know, big,
massive gaming companies

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.389
that I know.
-Do you debut them on Mixer,

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.890
or you just --
-Yeah, I can.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.126
Yeah, that's one of the things,
is I want to try to obviously

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.128
get a little bit more involved
in maybe another release

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:05.231
and possibly teasing things,
and, you know, pushing out

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:06.899
a lot of that early access
information,

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.968
like trailers and, you know --
-Do you play other games

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.603
besides, like, shooter games?
-Oh, absolutely.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.937
-You do?
-Yeah.

00:01:11.937 --> 00:01:14.073
-Have you ever played
"What Remains of Edith Finch"?

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.574
-I'm gonna give you --
I'm gonna raise that.

00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:17.443
Not raise it.
I'm going to match that.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.345
I want you to play a game
called "Until Dawn,"

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.848
because I know that "Until Dawn"
is an incredible game.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.415
-This is coming from Ninja.
I love it.

00:01:23.415 --> 00:01:25.085
"Until Dawn."
-Trust me.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.552
-Really?
-"Until Dawn," incredible game.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:29.455
And it's just, like, I feel
like, I need to play that game.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:31.857
-It's a P.O.V., like, you're
a girl, and you go into a house.

00:01:31.857 --> 00:01:34.227
-You're a girl. You're a guy.
I mean, you're everywhere.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.828
-Yes.
-You know, you're, like,

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.796
every single decision
that you make in the game

00:01:37.796 --> 00:01:39.765
is what's going to affect
what happens to someone else.

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.934
-It was, like -- It was like
reading a book, but it was game.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.370
-I need to play that game.
What's the game called?

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.172
-"What Remains of Edith Finch."

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.808
You're a yellow thing,
and you eat dots.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.243
And then ghosts chase after you.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.545
-Dude, that's great.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.646
-It sounds good, right?

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.214
No, no, it's a real game.
I swear to God.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:57.150
And you'll love it.
It's one of my favorite things.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.884
-Okay.
-It's gonna change your life.

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:00.919
-Alright.
-Speaking of changing your life,

00:02:00.919 --> 00:02:04.490
"Get Good: The Ultimate Guide
to Gaming," by Ninja.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.192
Dude, thank you
for writing this book.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.493
-Yeah, man.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.028
-How would you describe it?
It's not really, like,

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.064
a chapter book,
where you read start to finish.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.799
-Right, right, right.
Honestly, you know,

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.101
it's for people like you who
can, you know, if you read it,

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.569
you might be able to beat me
at a game on the show

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.603
every once and a while.

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:18.771
-Please, that's never
going to happen.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:19.872
-No, realistically, though --

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:22.741
-Yeah, thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:23.942
I try, though, I try.

00:02:23.942 --> 00:02:25.411
Why do I even try?
-It's okay, man.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.946
Realistically, though, I've been
streaming for nine years.

00:02:27.946 --> 00:02:30.449
I've been gaming for --
I'm, what, 28 now? Jesus.

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:32.251
I've been gaming for 18, 20
years of my entire --

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.752
-Since you were a baby. Stop.

00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:36.856
-Oh, my God. But my goal was --

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.258
There are so many people every
day, they ask me questions.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:40.292
"How can I stream?

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:41.827
How do I this?

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.896
How do I start this?"
-How do I set up a computer?

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:45.398
-And literally,
it's all in the book.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.099
-So this will be --
This will be --

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:50.303
This is like
when you're starting,

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.804
this will be your
kind of encyclopedia.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.439
-100%.
-You go here, and you go --

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:57.110
-There's everything you need to
learn about gaming, streaming.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.145
It's going to be in this book.
-There's also --

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:02.182
You debunk a lot of myths
that people have

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:04.049
about video games in general.
-Yes.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:05.851
-Like, one myth in there

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:09.955
is, like, "Do video games
cause violence?"

00:03:09.955 --> 00:03:11.324
-Ooh. It's a big question.

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.825
-I know.
-We're all talking about it.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:16.462
Just like there are movies that
have, you know, rated PG-13,

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.464
rated R, same thing
with video games.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.565
You know, your kids
shouldn't be playing

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.267
Rated M for Mature games.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.435
So as parents, it's up to you
guys to make sure

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:24.971
that you're watching and making
sure your kids aren't playing

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.573
those violent games
at a young age.

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:27.773
-Yeah.

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:28.941
How about the other myth

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:31.911
that "Video games
make your kids antisocial"?

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.613
-Oh, man. Listen, I would
honestly make the argument

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.082
that if you're
playing video games,

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.784
you are probably more social

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.953
than most people who aren't
playing video games.

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:41.286
I mean, I'm literally
talking to --

00:03:41.286 --> 00:03:43.189
You know, I mean, not only
am I talking to my friends

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.558
and my family and people who
are around me when I'm at home,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.426
but I'm also communicating
with people all across the world

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:49.762
and talking with my best friends
who live in New York.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.697
One lives in Nebraska.
One lives in Kansas.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.465
I'm talking to people all
the time. You know what I mean?

00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:54.767
-Do you meet up with these
people?

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.969
-Absolutely.
Yeah, at conventions

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:58.204
and gaming conventions

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:59.572
and tournaments
and things like that.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.307
-You married
one of these people?

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.243
-Oh, I mean, absolutely.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.944
-I mean, I technically did.
-Right?

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.112
-Yeah, my beautiful wife,
Jessica.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.546
-She's awesome.
But you guys were --

00:04:07.546 --> 00:04:09.548
Did you meet online, or you just
played together online?

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:11.284
-No, no, no. So, we met --

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.185
We didn't know one another.

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:14.654
But we met through video games.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.221
I went to a tournament.
It was called --

00:04:16.221 --> 00:04:17.456
It was in La Crosse, Wisconsin.

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.559
It was one of the worst
snowstorms in history.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.993
-Perfect for video games.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.562
Perfect for video games.
So, we get there.

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.397
I met her,
added her on Facebook,

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.899
and we stayed in touch
for, you know, four years.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.667
And then finally
we were both single.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.302
And now we're married. Happily.

00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:31.970
-Happily married. Absolutely.
She's the best.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.439
That's her backstage.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.241
[ Applause ]
Happily married.

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.877
You have this. You're on Mixer.
You have a book.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.712
-Yes.
-And then, crazier news,

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.881
you just signed a deal
with Adidas.

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.181
-Yes.
-Like --

00:04:43.181 --> 00:04:44.783
-Right here. Time in.

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.252
-I mean, what's going on?

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.921
-I can honestly say, I think,
I recently did a shoot with --

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.289
I don't think I can say it yet,

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:53.259
but I did a shoot about Adidas
with somebody.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.827
And we talked about -- You know,
they asked that question

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:58.898
like, "Your 13-year-old self,
did you imagine

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.899
ever signing anything
with Adidas whatsoever?"

00:05:00.899 --> 00:05:02.167
And it's like, "No,
I was playing soccer

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.470
using their stuff.
But I was not by any means like,

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.406
'One day, one day, I'm going
to have my own clothes and --'"

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:10.042
It's like, no.
It's mind-boggling.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.677
-What's next?
What do you want to do next?

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:13.212
I mean, is there --
Do you have goals?

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.880
What -- You're crushing
everything.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.182
-Thank you, man.
I would say, what's next?

00:05:17.182 --> 00:05:18.584
I can't say anything
specifically.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:19.652
-Okay.
-But for people

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.986
who are watching,
just keep an eye out

00:05:20.986 --> 00:05:24.256
on all the screens,
both big and small.

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:26.859
-Really? Movies and TV?

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.627
Are you -- Wow. No, no, no.

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:31.097
Wasn't that impressive
that I guessed what that was?

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.398
-That was incredible.
That was amazing.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.766
-Thank you.
Are you going to host --

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.100
Are you going to host
a talk show?

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.602
-I would absolutely love to.
But unfortunately,

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:38.170
I feel like there's a lot
of top talent out there.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:39.639
So I'm going to wait.
I'm going to wide it out.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.107
I'm going to wait it out.
I'm going to wait

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:43.209
till all the guys dip out.
-That was a nice compliment.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:45.745
I love you. Thank you.
Tyler "Ninja" Blevins.

